Requirements: 29   with obligations: 28   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] `parse_task_file` walks the top-level nodes of the parsed task file and spans
    each list item using `_inline_content`, which returns the first inline node it finds
    and stops. A list item whose content is a paragraph followed by a nested bullet list
    therefore yields the first paragraph's text, that text is located in the source, and
    the narrow span is accepted. The nested list is never visited. The same happens to a
    second paragraph inside a single list item, and to any block nested inside a claimed
    item — a nested code fence, a nested table.
    -> obligation-parse-nested-content-as-own-or-unread  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-02, task-05, constraint-01, exclusion-01, exclusion-03)
       Nested content under a claimed list item is accounted for either as its own
       requirement or as unread source, so it is never omitted from both registry and
       unclaimed coverage.
    -> obligation-second-paragraph-as-own-or-unread  [functional/explicit]   (also serves constraint-02)
       A second or subsequent paragraph inside a single list item is accounted for
       either as its own requirement or as unread source.
    -> obligation-no-unaccounted-region-for-nested-bullet-item  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-03)
       A list item containing a nested bullet list contributes no unaccounted region.
    -> obligation-no-unaccounted-region-for-multi-paragraph-item  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-04)
       A list item containing two paragraphs contributes no unaccounted region.

[task-02] The widening fallback in `_span` fires only when the inline text cannot be
    found in the source. Here it is found, so the fallback never runs.
    -> obligation-parse-nested-content-as-own-or-unread  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01, task-05, constraint-01, exclusion-01, exclusion-03)
       Nested content under a claimed list item is accounted for either as its own
       requirement or as unread source, so it is never omitted from both registry and
       unclaimed coverage.

[task-03] Because the item was claimed, the dropped content reaches neither the registry
    nor `unclaimed`. It produces no requirement id, receives no disposition, and cannot
    be recorded as unaccounted for, because no registry entry exists for it.
    `unread_source` is therefore empty and the CLI prints `unaccounted for: 0`.
    -> obligation-unclaimed-covers-all-task-file-text  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-04, constraint-04, constraint-10, exclusion-04, exclusion-05)
       unclaimed accounts for all task-file text, including text beyond unrecognised
       top-level headings.
    -> obligation-every-non-whitespace-non-heading-region-accounted  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves task-04, task-05, constraint-05)
       Every non-whitespace, non-heading region of a task file is covered by either a
       registry span or an unclaimed span.

[task-04] #202 established that a parse may only be authoritative if it reports what it
    missed, and taught readers to trust that zero. This drop occurs under a clean bill
    of health, which is worse than a drop under no bill of health at all.
    -> obligation-unclaimed-covers-all-task-file-text  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-03, constraint-04, constraint-10, exclusion-04, exclusion-05)
       unclaimed accounts for all task-file text, including text beyond unrecognised
       top-level headings.
    -> obligation-every-non-whitespace-non-heading-region-accounted  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves task-03, task-05, constraint-05)
       Every non-whitespace, non-heading region of a task file is covered by either a
       registry span or an unclaimed span.

[task-05] Decide whether nested content under a claimed list item is a requirement in
    its own right or a continuation of its parent, then make the parse account for every
    region of the task file: each one is either inside a registry span or inside an
    unclaimed span, and never inside neither.
    -> obligation-parse-nested-content-as-own-or-unread  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01, task-02, constraint-01, exclusion-01, exclusion-03)
       Nested content under a claimed list item is accounted for either as its own
       requirement or as unread source, so it is never omitted from both registry and
       unclaimed coverage.
    -> obligation-every-non-whitespace-non-heading-region-accounted  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves task-03, task-04, constraint-05)
       Every non-whitespace, non-heading region of a task file is covered by either a
       registry span or an unclaimed span.

[constraint-01] Nested content under a claimed list item is extracted as its own
    requirement, or reported as unread. It is never absent from both.
    -> obligation-parse-nested-content-as-own-or-unread  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01, task-02, task-05, exclusion-01, exclusion-03)
       Nested content under a claimed list item is accounted for either as its own
       requirement or as unread source, so it is never omitted from both registry and
